message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "Everettian Probability in Lean: Refinement-Invariant Rational Expectation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dalimier
    given-names: Bertrand
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    city: Nogent-sur-Marne
    country: FR
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-2457-375X"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization with stable conditional and exact-finite
  public APIs. It represents rational values by Born expectation under
  explicit premises, characterizes same records by unitary orbits, realizes
  compatible fine-weight profiles while preserving present records and
  consequences, and gives calibrated continuator credences with explicit
  zero-parent-fibre treatment. The journal-audit layer additionally supplies
  typed relative-necessity witnesses for exposed Born-calibration premises,
  formulation-minimality lemmas, and a dimension-two boundary witness for the
  one-directional Uhlhorn interface. The scope is finite-dimensional and
  projective; it provides neither approximate decoherence nor a natural local
  Hamiltonian, and does not derive rationality from unitary dynamics alone.
keywords:
  - quantum foundations
  - Born rule
  - Everett interpretation
  - decision theory
  - Gleason theorem
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
